    "status": "present",
    "value": "Return at most ten times the array length prefix-reversal lengths that sort the supplied permutation. Preserve the input array. The approach is: move each remaining maximum to its final position with at most two prefix flips on a copy. Its target cost is O(n^2) time/O(n) space; at most2n flips. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
